    {
      "id": "claim_9529837e760e4f61b001d5aaaca512e3",
      "statement": "The migration_cursor field enables crash-safe in-place format upgrades: during migration, format_version still reads legacy (1) while inode IDs < migration_cursor hold v2 records; readers dispatch per-inode via inode_record_version_for(), and cursor is persisted after each rewritten inode (slot flushed, cursor advanced, superblock persisted, block 0 flushed). On completion, format_version updates to 2 (FORMAT_VERSION_FIXED_INODE) and cursor clears to 0.",
